        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d313ce77-7cc2-559c-8b9a-5f526f5c789f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Travis McGee, John D. MacDonald, Janet Evanovich, Stephanie Plum, Steffie Hall\n- Products: Travis McGee books, Stephanie Plum novels\n- Concepts: title themes in detective/mystery fiction, bestseller lists\n\nFacts:\n- Travis McGee is a fictional character created by American mystery writer John D. MacDonald.\n- The 21 Travis McGee books all use a color in their titles, making the series an early example of a detective or mystery fiction series with a title theme.\n- Janet Evanovich began her career by writing short contemporary romance novels under the pen name Steffie Hall.\n- Janet Evanovich became famous for writing contemporary mystery novels about Stephanie Plum, a former lingerie buyer from Trenton, New Jersey, who becomes a bounty hunter after losing her job.\n- Janet Evanovich's Stephanie Plum novels have appeared on The New York Times, USA Today, The Wall Street Journal, and Amazon bestseller lists.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
